  Vulnerability: Industry surveys (e.g., McKinsey, Gartner) do document high AI project failure rates, and many practitioners confirm integration bottlenecks — meaning this belief has reasonably strong anecdotal and survey-based support; the strongest counter is that failure modes are heterogeneous and attributing them primarily to the integration stage rather than to poor problem selection, data quality, or talent gaps may itself be an oversimplification that obscures more actionable root causes.
