e inspection.\n\nWho answers when procurement-linked screening filters out every open-source alternative and leaves federal agencies tethered to a single proprietary vendor? The historical record of comparable technology procurement shows that compliance gates consistently consolidate market power while providing little measurable protection against the harms experienced by affected populations. Procurement officers sign the contracts, the dominant platform profits from guaranteed public sector revenue, and marginalized communities absorb the downstream costs of automated discrimination. Pretending that procurement contracts neutralize incumbent protectionism ignores the observable mechanics of how institutional purchasing power is captured by the regulated entities.",
